{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791567578,"nonce":"ppTC7627t88+f+u4A0wPWlBLZ5k=","message":"Fixed locally in f72b41453ebef366b5415f86b50c66167ba241f5, not pushed.\n\nThe layout sync now compares each text node's overrides (font size, line height, weight, style, letter spacing) with what the node was last measured at, and on a change refreshes the measure context, the fixed size of a non-wrapping node, the baseline the builder reported, and the node's own measured width, ascender and half-leading. Non-wrapping text, which has no measure context, is resized through its style.\n\nWhat it turned up beyond the box size: paint draws the overridden font size but used the build-time ascender, so a CSS font-size put the baseline in the wrong place. For 32px text the offset was 13.69 against 31.29 from the face, a 17.6px error (test an_overridden_size_carries_the_baseline_of_that_size). Letter-spacing on non-wrapping text now widens its box too.\n\nTests: crates/blinc_layout/tests/text_overrides.rs, 7 tests; with the sync disabled six fail, and only the \"left as built\" guard passes.\n\nThe prediction in this issue that cn would move did not hold. A capture of buttons, badges, label, kbd, alert, card, progress and a table under cn's real stylesheet and theme variables was identical before and after, in node bounds and in pixels. cn sets its text sizes fluently at build, and a CSS font-size rule on a cn class lands on the container: font-size is not inherited into the text node by the stylesheet pass, so no text node carries an override. So cn text whose size a rule is meant to set still does not follow it. That is a separate gap (font-size inheritance), not fixed here.\n\nOne thing seen in that capture and not investigated: the table header text \"Name\" wrapped to \"Nam\" and \"e\" at a 900px width.","files":null}]}